{"entries":[{"timestamp":1792201582135,"editorVersion":"9.1.1","changes":[{"type":"edited","filename":"pxt.json","patch":[{"start1":501,"length1":35,"diffs":[[1,"    \"preferredEditor\": \"tsprj\"\n"]]}]},{"type":"edited","filename":"main.ts","patch":[{"start1":595,"length1":61,"diffs":[[1,"\n// ---------------- Line follower ----------------\n\n// The line sensor has four eyes in a row under the front of the robot.\n// Asking it over I2C gives one bit per eye: bit 0 is the left eye,\n// bit 3 is the right eye. A 1 means that eye sees the black line.\nfunction readSensors(): number {\n    pins.i2cWriteNumber(0x1a, 4, NumberFormat.Int8LE)\n    return pins.i2cReadNumber(0x1a, NumberFormat.UInt8LE, false) & 0b1111\n}\n\n// Where the line is, for each pattern the sensor can show.\n// 0 means the line is under the middle of the robot. Positive means\n// the line is to the LEFT, so the robot should turn left. Negative\n// means it is to the right. The pictures are left to right, with a #\n// where an eye sees the line.\nconst NO_LINE = 99\nconst LINE_POSITION = [\n    NO_LINE,  // ....  no line\n    3,        // #...  far left\n    1,        // .#..  a little left\n    2,        // ##..  left\n    -1,       // ..#.  a little right\n    NO_LINE,  // #.#.  makes no sense\n    0,        // .##.  centred\n    1,        // ###.  wide line, a little left\n    -3,       // ...#  far right\n    NO_LINE,  // #..#  makes no sense\n    NO_LINE,  // .#.#  makes no sense\n    NO_LINE,  // ##.#  makes no sense\n    -2,       // ..##  right\n    NO_LINE,  // #.##  makes no sense\n    -1,       // .###  wide line, a little right\n    0,        // ####  centred on a wide line\n]\n\nconst SPEED = 15  // cm/s\nconst KP = 40     // how hard to turn: degrees per second of turning for each step the line is off centre\nconst KD = 0      // how much to resist sudden changes; leave at 0 until KP is working\n\nlet running = false\n\nfunction followLine() {\n    running = true\n    let lastPosition = 0\n    diffDrive.driveTwist(SPEED, 0)\n    while (diffDrive.driveTick() && running) {\n        let position = LINE_POSITION[readSensors()]\n        // Lost the line? Keep turning the way we were already turning.\n        if (position == NO_LINE) position = lastPosition\n        const turn = KP * position + KD * (position - lastPosition)\n        diffDrive.driveTwist(SPEED, turn)\n        lastPosition = position\n    }\n    diffDrive.stop()\n}\n\n// A starts following the line, B stops.\ninput.onButtonPressed(Button.A, followLine)\ninput.onButtonPressed(Button.B, function () {\n    running = false\n"]]}]}]}],"snapshots":[{"timestamp":1792201582134,"editorVersion":"9.1.1","text":{"main.blocks":"<xml xmlns=\"https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml\"><variables></variables><block type=\"pxt-on-start\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"><statement name=\"HANDLER\"><block type=\"diffDrive_setupRobot\"><next><block type=\"diffDrive_setupRadio\"><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">tigez configuration\nradio channel, group</comment><value name=\"channel\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">52</field></shadow></value><value name=\"group\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">179</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"diffDrive_setupWifi\"><data>{\"commentRefs\":[],\"fieldData\":{}}</data><value name=\"ssid\"><shadow type=\"text\"><field name=\"TEXT\">Robot_Garage</field></shadow></value><value name=\"password\"><shadow type=\"text\"><field name=\"TEXT\">code4life2006</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"diffDrive_setWheelCalibration\"><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">wheel diameter 91.04 mm</comment><value name=\"calib\"><block type=\"math_arithmetic\"><field name=\"OP\">DIVIDE</field><value name=\"A\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0</field></shadow><block type=\"math_arithmetic\"><field name=\"OP\">MULTIPLY</field><value name=\"A\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">91.04</field></shadow></value><value name=\"B\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0</field></shadow><block type=\"Math__constant\"><field name=\"MEMBER\">Math.PI</field></block></value></block></value><value name=\"B\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">360</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type=\"diffDrive_setTrackWidth\"><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">effective track width, cm (not measured with a ruler)</comment><value name=\"width\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">11.62</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"diffDrive_setConfigValue\"><field name=\"field\">ConfigField.RotationalSlip</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">from the rotation calibration</comment><value name=\"value\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">0.9829</field></shadow></value><next><block type=\"diffDrive_setMotorPorts\"><field name=\"left\">MotorPort.M1</field><field name=\"right\">MotorPort.M2</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">left wheel motor port, right wheel motor port</comment><next><block type=\"diffDrive_setWheelMultiplier\"><field name=\"side\">MotorSide.Left</field><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">left wheel speed multiplier</comment><value name=\"value\"><shadow type=\"math_number\"><field name=\"NUM\">1</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block><block type=\"device_forever\" x=\"711\" y=\"0\"><comment pinned=\"false\" h=\"80\" w=\"160\">left wheel speed multiplier</comment></block></xml>","main.ts":"diffDrive.setupRobot()\n// tigez configuration\n// radio channel, group\ndiffDrive.setupRadio(52, 179)\ndiffDrive.setupWifi(\"Robot_Garage\", \"code4life2006\")\n// wheel diameter 91.04 mm\ndiffDrive.setWheelCalibration(91.04 * Math.PI / 360)\n// effective track width, cm (not measured with a ruler)\ndiffDrive.setTrackWidth(11.62)\n// from the rotation calibration\ndiffDrive.setConfigValue(ConfigField.RotationalSlip, 0.9829)\n// left wheel motor port, right wheel motor port\ndiffDrive.setMotorPorts(MotorPort.M1, MotorPort.M2)\n// left wheel speed multiplier\ndiffDrive.setWheelMultiplier(MotorSide.Left, 1)\n\n// ---------------- Line follower ----------------\n\n// The line sensor has four eyes in a row under the front of the robot.\n// Asking it over I2C gives one bit per eye: bit 0 is the left eye,\n// bit 3 is the right eye. A 1 means that eye sees the black line.\nfunction readSensors(): number {\n    pins.i2cWriteNumber(0x1a, 4, NumberFormat.Int8LE)\n    return pins.i2cReadNumber(0x1a, NumberFormat.UInt8LE, false) & 0b1111\n}\n\n// Where the line is, for each pattern the sensor can show.\n// 0 means the line is under the middle of the robot. Positive means\n// the line is to the LEFT, so the robot should turn left. Negative\n// means it is to the right. The pictures are left to right, with a #\n// where an eye sees the line.\nconst NO_LINE = 99\nconst LINE_POSITION = [\n    NO_LINE,  // ....  no line\n    3,        // #...  far left\n    1,        // .#..  a little left\n    2,        // ##..  left\n    -1,       // ..#.  a little right\n    NO_LINE,  // #.#.  makes no sense\n    0,        // .##.  centred\n    1,        // ###.  wide line, a little left\n    -3,       // ...#  far right\n    NO_LINE,  // #..#  makes no sense\n    NO_LINE,  // .#.#  makes no sense\n    NO_LINE,  // ##.#  makes no sense\n    -2,       // ..##  right\n    NO_LINE,  // #.##  makes no sense\n    -1,       // .###  wide line, a little right\n    0,        // ####  centred on a wide line\n]\n\nconst SPEED = 15  // cm/s\nconst KP = 40     // how hard to turn: degrees per second of turning for each step the line is off centre\nconst KD = 0      // how much to resist sudden changes; leave at 0 until KP is working\n\nlet running = false\n\nfunction followLine() {\n    running = true\n    let lastPosition = 0\n    diffDrive.driveTwist(SPEED, 0)\n    while (diffDrive.driveTick() && running) {\n        let position = LINE_POSITION[readSensors()]\n        // Lost the line? Keep turning the way we were already turning.\n        if (position == NO_LINE) position = lastPosition\n        const turn = KP * position + KD * (position - lastPosition)\n        diffDrive.driveTwist(SPEED, turn)\n        lastPosition = position\n    }\n    diffDrive.stop()\n}\n\n// A starts following the line, B stops.\ninput.onButtonPressed(Button.A, followLine)\ninput.onButtonPressed(Button.B, function () {\n    running = false\n})\n","README.md":"\n> Open this page at [https://ericbusboom.github.io/tigez/](https://ericbusboom.github.io/tigez/)\n\n## Use as Extension\n\nThis repository can be added as an **extension** in MakeCode.\n\n* open [https://makecode.microbit.org/](https://makecode.microbit.org/)\n* click on **New Project**\n* click on **Extensions** under the gearwheel menu\n* search for **https://github.com/ericbusboom/tigez** and import\n\n## Edit this project\n\nTo edit this repository in MakeCode.\n\n* open [https://makecode.microbit.org/](https://makecode.microbit.org/)\n* click on **Import** then click on **Import URL**\n* paste **https://github.com/ericbusboom/tigez** and click import\n\n## Local development\n\nBuild, flash and edit from this folder instead of the website. You need\n[Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) 20+ and the pxt CLI (`npm install -g pxt`).\n\n```sh\nmake setup      # npm install (micro:bit target) + pxt install (extensions)\nmake build      # compile to built/binary.hex\nmake deploy     # build and copy the hex to a plugged-in micro:bit\nmake code       # open this project in the local MakeCode editor, in Chrome\n```\n\n`npm run setup`, `npm run build`, `npm run deploy` and `npm run code` do the\nsame things.\n\n### The local editor\n\n`make code` runs [scripts/code.sh](scripts/code.sh), which starts `pxt serve`\nand opens Google Chrome on this project. Chrome matters: flashing from the\neditor's Download button uses WebUSB, which only Chromium browsers have.\n\nPlain `pxt serve` is not enough. It serves the editor from\n`node_modules/pxt-microbit`, opens the default browser, and shows an empty\nproject list, because the editor keeps its own projects in the browser unless\nthe URL asks for the filesystem workspace. The script links this repo into\n`projects/`, writes `.header.json` so the project has a stable id, and opens\n`http://localhost:3232/index.html?ws=fs#header:<id>&local_token=...`. Edits in\nthe editor save straight back to `main.ts` and `main.blocks` here.\n\npxt always uses ports 3232 and 3233, so a server left running in any other\nproject blocks this one with `EADDRINUSE`. The script reports the offending\nprocess and how to kill it. To find it by hand:\n\n```sh\nlsof -nP -t -iTCP:3233 -sTCP:LISTEN | xargs kill\n```\n\n#### Metadata (used for search, rendering)\n\n* for PXT/microbit\n<script src=\"https://makecode.com/gh-pages-embed.js\"></script><script>makeCodeRender(\"{{ site.makecode.home_url }}\", \"{{ site.github.owner_name }}/{{ site.github.repository_name }}\");</script>\n","pxt.json":"{\n    \"name\": \"Tigez\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"dependencies\": {\n        \"core\": \"*\",\n        \"radio\": \"*\",\n        \"microphone\": \"*\",\n        \"nezha-diffdrive\": \"github:League-Robotics/pxt-nezha-diffdrive#v1.20261006.1\"\n    },\n    \"files\": [\n        \"main.blocks\",\n        \"main.ts\",\n        \"README.md\"\n    ],\n    \"testFiles\": [\n        \"test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"targetVersions\": {\n        \"target\": \"9.0.12\",\n        \"targetId\": \"microbit\"\n    },\n    \"supportedTargets\": [\n        \"microbit\"\n    ],\n    \"preferredEditor\": \"tsprj\"\n}\n","test.ts":"// tests go here; this will not be compiled when this package is used as an extension.\n"}}],"shares":[],"lastSaveTime":1792201582135}